SUMMARY:Kokedama
LOCATION:181 Fremont - Level 39, Residents’ Club
DESCRIPTION:The Japanese art of moss ball gardening. You’ll wrap a living plant in nutrient-rich soil and soft moss to make a kokedama, a sculptural piece that sits on a shelf or hangs by a window.\n\nWe begin with a demonstration, then everyone makes their own. All supplies and care instructions are provided, and no experience is needed.\n\nLight bites and wine will be served throughout. You’ll take home your kokedama, and everything you need to keep it thriving.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
